  "setup_prompt": "Set up Product factory 0.1.5, an OpenRig factory from rigs.to.\n\n1. Download the archive and check its hash before unpacking. The sha256 must be exactly d4c49ba28c1983dfcdfa64a87bb91771e28c4ca98369248cbc6276458b8ad224:\n   curl -fLO https://github.com/mvschwarz/rigs-to-apps/releases/download/product-factory-v0.1.5/product-factory-0.1.5.tar.gz\n   echo \"d4c49ba28c1983dfcdfa64a87bb91771e28c4ca98369248cbc6276458b8ad224  product-factory-0.1.5.tar.gz\" | shasum -a 256 -c\n2. Unpack it somewhere stable and read SETUP.md inside before running anything:\n   mkdir -p ~/rig-factories && tar -xzf product-factory-0.1.5.tar.gz -C ~/rig-factories\n   cd ~/rig-factories/product-factory-0.1.5\n3. Follow SETUP.md with the OpenRig I already run (leave my other rigs and its kernel alone): run\n   node launch.mjs --project <dir> --plan-only, explain to me every permission change it prints, and launch only\n   after I agree. Never pipe anything into a shell."
